  "summary": "These passages use light to portray guidance, revelation, and a life turned toward God. Psalm 27 calls the Lord its light and salvation; John 1 presents life and light shining in darkness; Ephesians 5 urges readers who were darkness to live as children of light; 1 John 1 contrasts walking in light with denying sin. The image moves from trust to revelation and ethical response, and the Hebrew psalm provides a related image rather than an occurrence of the Greek term named here.",
  "historical_context": "The references include a psalm of trust, the opening of John’s Gospel, and instructions in Ephesians and 1 John. These literary settings explain the distinct uses of the image; no separate historical comparison or lexical range is claimed.",
