  "literary_context": "Psalm 27 is a prayer of confidence, John 1 is a prologue, and Ephesians and 1 John use exhortation and contrast. Light names security in the psalm, revelation in John, and an ethical way of life in the letters. These forms help prevent a single symbolic meaning from being imposed everywhere.",
  "covenantal_significance": "The texts connect God’s light with protection and with a life marked by truth and changed conduct. John’s image of light entering darkness and the letters’ call to walk in light encourage readers to notice both divine initiative and human response.",
